---
title: Lotka-Volterra Work-Precision Diagrams
author: Chris Rackauckas
---

## Lotka-Volterra

The purpose of this problem is to test the performance on easy problems. Since it's periodic, the error is naturally low, and so most of the difference will come down to startup times and, when measuring the interpolations, the algorithm choices.

```julia
using OrdinaryDiffEq, ParameterizedFunctions, ODEInterfaceDiffEq, LSODA,
      Sundials, DiffEqDevTools, StaticArrays, OrdinaryDiffEqSIMDRK, IRKGaussLegendre
using OrdinaryDiffEqAdamsBashforthMoulton, OrdinaryDiffEqExtrapolation, OrdinaryDiffEqHighOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqLowOrderRK
using SciMLLogging

f = @ode_def LotkaVolterra begin
    dx = a*x - b*x*y
    dy = -c*y + d*x*y
end a b c d

p = SA[1.5, 1.0, 3.0, 1.0]
prob = ODEProblem{true, SciMLBase.FullSpecialize}(f, [1.0; 1.0], (0.0, 10.0), p)
probstatic = ODEProblem{false}(f, SA[1.0; 1.0], (0.0, 10.0), p)

abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (6:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (3:10);
sol = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14)
sol2 = solve(probstatic, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14)
sol_endpoint = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14,
    save_everystep = false, dense = false)
sol2_endpoint = solve(probstatic, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14,
    save_everystep = false, dense = false)
probs = [prob, probstatic]
test_sol_dense = [sol, sol2]
test_sol = [sol_endpoint, sol2_endpoint];
using Plots;
gr()
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "..", "workprecision_table.jl"))

const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR = 1.0e-14
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SIMD_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :simd_rk, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff, :rhs_calls_unavailable]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS = [:irkgl, :implicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS = [LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS..., :simd]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS = [:sundials, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:sundials, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_LSODA_TAGS = [:lsoda, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS = [LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS..., :static]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [LOTKA_VOLTERRA_MULTISTEP_TAGS..., :static]
const LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_SIMD_RK_TAGS = [LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SIMD_RK_TAGS..., :static]

function assert_work_table_identities(wps)
    @assert length(wps.wps) == length(wps.setups)
    for i in eachindex(wps.wps), j in 1:(i - 1)
        duplicate = isequal(wps.wps[i].name, wps.wps[j].name) &&
            isequal(wps.wps[i].tags, wps.wps[j].tags)
        @assert !duplicate "duplicate (Algorithm, Tags) pair in work-table rows $j and $i"
    end
    for (setup, wp) in zip(wps.setups, wps.wps)
        alg = setup[:alg]
        if isequal(alg, IRKGL16(simd = true))
            @assert :simd in wp.tags "SIMD IRKGL16 lacks the :simd variant tag"
        elseif isequal(alg, IRKGL16(simd = false))
            @assert :simd ∉ wp.tags "scalar IRKGL16 unexpectedly has the :simd variant tag"
        end
        if get(setup, :prob_choice, nothing) == 2
            @assert :static in wp.tags "static setup lacks the :static variant tag"
        else
            @assert :static ∉ wp.tags "dynamic setup unexpectedly has the :static variant tag"
        end
    end
    for tag in (:simd, :static, :rhs_calls_unavailable)
        @assert tag_kind(tag) !== :family "$tag must not change plot-family grouping"
    end
    return nothing
end
```

Each sweep requests only the error metrics needed for its measurement with
`error_estimates` and attaches solver metadata tags to the results. The table
with each work-precision figure reports the best endpoint error, that point's
timing, right-hand-side calls, accepted steps, and a computed refinement rate
when the tolerance grid resolves one. Rate calculations exclude errors at or
below `1e-14`, the tolerance used to construct each numerical endpoint reference;
an em dash means that the rate or counter is unavailable or unresolved. Under RHS
calls, the dash in SIMD-RK rows means "RHS-call count not reported: SIMD invocation
unit is ambiguous". The plotted reference trajectories retain dense output because
the figures and interpolation-error references consume them; the endpoint references
use endpoint-only output.

```julia
plot(sol)
```

### Low Order

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode45()) # fail
          Dict(:alg=>dopri5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>MER5v2(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_SIMD_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>MER6v2(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_SIMD_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>RK6v4(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_SIMD_RK_TAGS)]
low_order_setups = setups
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol,
    error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), maxiters = 10000, numruns = 100)
low_order_wp = wp
low_order_abstols = abstols
low_order_reltols = reltols
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

Here we see the OrdinaryDiffEq.jl algorithms once again far in the lead.

### Interpolation Error

Since the problem is periodic, the real measure of error is the error throughout the solution.

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode45())
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(
    probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol_dense, error_estimates = [:final, :l2, :L2], maxiters = 10000,
    error_estimate = :L2, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

Here we see the power of algorithm-specific interpolations: the OrdinaryDiffEq.jl methods reach $L^2$ errors below $10^{-10}$ throughout the solution, while `IRKGL16` stays at errors many orders of magnitude larger at every tolerance. The pinned IRKGaussLegendre v1.0.4 builds its solution without an interpolant, so `sol(t)` falls back to a linear interpolation between its accepted steps, and since a 16th-order method resolves this problem in a few dozen steps, the dense error sits at about $10^{-1}$ however small the endpoint error gets. Dense output for `IRKGL16` is being added upstream in [IRKGaussLegendre.jl#150](https://github.com/SciML/IRKGaussLegendre.jl/pull/150).

## Higher Order

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP8(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>dop853(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode78()) # fails
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol,
    error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), maxiters = 1000, numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>odex(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ddeabm(), :tags=>[LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS..., :accepted_steps_unavailable])
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>CVODE_Adams(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>lsoda(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_LSODA_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ARKODE(Sundials.Explicit(), order = 6), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol,
    error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), maxiters = 1000, numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

Again we look at interpolations:

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP8(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode78())
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol_dense, error_estimates = [:final, :l2, :L2], dense = true,
    maxiters = 1000, error_estimate = :L2, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

Again, `IRKGL16` suffers when measuring the interpolations because its `sol(t)` is only a linear interpolation between steps, while the Verner methods, which have algorithm-specific interpolations of matching order, keep their accuracy between the timesteps.

## Comparison with Non-RK methods

Now let's test Tsit5 and Vern9 against parallel extrapolation methods and an
Adams-Bashforth-Moulton:

```julia
abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (8:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (8:13)
setups = [Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>VCABM(), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_IRKGL_SIMD_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>VCABM(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_STATIC_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>AitkenNeville(min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)]
solnames = ["Tsit5", "Vern9", "VCABM", "IRKGL16", "IRKGL16 SIMD",
    "Vern9 Static", "VCABM Static",
    "AitkenNeville", "Midpoint Deuflhard", "Midpoint Hairer Wanner"]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(
    probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final], names = solnames,
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 9, threading = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = false), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4,
              sequence = :romberg, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4,
              sequence = :bulirsch, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)]
solnames = ["Deuflhard", "No threads", "standard", "Romberg", "Bulirsch"]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(
    probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final], names = solnames,
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
assert_work_table_identities(wp)
print_work_table(wp, LOTKA_VOLTERRA_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 10, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>LOTKA_VOLTERRA_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
